meta {
  name: Update Backlog Entry
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

put {
  url: {{backendUrl}}/api/backlog/entries/{{entryId}}
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{authToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "status": "Completed",
    "playtime": 140,
    "review_stars": 5,
    "review": "Incredible open world design."
  }
}

docs {
  review_stars is 0-10 (values outside that range are a 400).
  trailer_link, if sent, must be a canonical YouTube watch URL
  (https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=<11-char id>), anything else is a 400.
  Partially updates a backlog entry - only the fields present in the
  body are changed, everything else is left as-is. Sending a field as
  explicit null clears it (where nullable); omitting it entirely leaves
  it unchanged. Run auth/Login and "Create Backlog Entry" first so
  entryId is set.

  404 if the entry doesn't exist or isn't owned by the caller. genre/
  platform, if sent, follow the same comma-rejection rule as "Create
  Backlog Entry".
}
